-- the 2×2 on (φ₀, φ₁): h00 = 0 (the vacuum's Coulomb zero and no self-hop), h01 = −2t (four hops of amplitude 1
-- into the normalized shell, halved), h11 = 3L/4. Its determinant is h00·h11 − h01² = −4t² < 0 for t > 0, so it has
-- one negative eigenvalue; with h00 = 0 and h11 > 0 the lowest is (h11 − √(h11² + 4·4t²))/2 < 0. The molecular
-- ground E₀ ≤ this < 0 = the separated atoms (chem/h2-net), for every t > 0: H₂ binds. The determinant's sign for
-- free t, as a polynomial identity:  h00·h11 − (2t)² + 4t² = 0  with h00 = 0.
h2-det : (A : Type) → (A → A → A) → (A → A → A) → (BQ → A) → List A → A × A
h2-det A ad mu q vs = (λ g → (ad (mu (q (fn-q 0 1)) (g 1)) (mu (q (fn-nq 1 1)) (mu (mu (q (fn-q 2 1)) (g 0)) (mu (q (fn-q 2 1)) (g 0)))) , mu (q (fn-nq 4 1)) (mu (g 0) (g 0)))) (λ i → al-nth A (q (fn-q 0 1)) i vs)
